WEBVTT

00:00:13.810 --> 00:00:15.950
I couldn’t do anything.

00:00:15.950 --> 00:00:20.950
I’ll hunt your Number and your soul!

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:24.880
I can’t beat him.

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:29.000
I clearly lost that battle.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:32.340
I’ll hunt your soul!

00:00:32.780 --> 00:00:36.220
Go, Galaxy-Eyes Photon Dragon!

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:38.930
Photon Stream of De—

00:00:38.930 --> 00:00:41.390
We’ll continue this duel later!

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:52.190
If he didn’t stop the duel, I would’ve vanished.

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:01.910
Ouch...

00:01:06.430 --> 00:01:08.170
Astral...

00:01:09.760 --> 00:01:16.130
There’s a guy after my soul
because you possessed me.

00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:19.190
I’m sorry.

00:01:20.210 --> 00:01:21.600
C’mon!

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:23.660
Stop being depressed!

00:01:23.660 --> 00:01:27.810
We have to defeat Kaito
in order to survive!

00:01:30.820 --> 00:01:33.570
Can I win?

00:01:33.570 --> 00:01:37.410
Stop being unsure!
You have to win!

00:01:37.410 --> 00:01:38.320
This isn’t just about you—

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:39.870
Yuma!

00:01:39.870 --> 00:01:42.620
Kotori! Tetsuo!

00:01:43.950 --> 00:01:46.790
World Duel Carnival?

00:01:46.790 --> 00:01:49.430
Yeah, WDC for short.

00:01:49.430 --> 00:01:52.000
It’s going to take place at Heartland.

00:01:52.490 --> 00:01:58.470
Powerful duelists from around
the world will be at the Carnival!

00:01:59.140 --> 00:02:01.430
That means he’ll be there.

00:02:01.950 --> 00:02:03.140
Yuma...

00:02:05.140 --> 00:02:08.140
Yuma, what’s wrong?

00:02:08.140 --> 00:02:09.900
Yuma.

00:02:11.010 --> 00:02:12.650
Grandma!

00:02:12.650 --> 00:02:18.570
I want you to run a small errand for me.

00:02:18.570 --> 00:02:20.410
This?

00:02:20.410 --> 00:02:23.280
I don’t feel like it.

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:29.150
Where did my obedient grandson go?

00:02:29.150 --> 00:02:34.130
I’m right here!

00:02:54.570 --> 00:02:59.530
Grandma, this isn’t a small errand!

00:03:00.360 --> 00:03:02.680
I can’t walk anymore!

00:03:04.260 --> 00:03:07.280
Yuma, you’re pathetic.

00:03:07.280 --> 00:03:10.270
You’ve given up on kattobing?

00:03:10.270 --> 00:03:11.290
What?

00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:14.720
Nothing’s impossible when I kattobing!

00:03:14.720 --> 00:03:18.720
I’m kattobing!

00:03:20.440 --> 00:03:22.190
All right!

00:03:30.420 --> 00:03:32.770
Is anyone here?

00:03:33.440 --> 00:03:35.940
This place is filthy.

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:45.620
Yuma?

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:49.630
It’s a monkey!

00:03:49.630 --> 00:03:51.910
Right there!

00:03:53.990 --> 00:03:56.090
Welcome, cutie.

00:03:56.640 --> 00:03:59.050
It’s not a monkey. It’s an old man.

00:04:08.220 --> 00:04:11.730
Whether it’s rain, wind, blizzard or the scorching sun

00:04:11.730 --> 00:04:14.850
They give color to each day
Will and love keep me from losing heart

00:04:14.850 --> 00:04:17.440
Your kindness was harsh
I learned frustration when we clashed

00:04:17.650 --> 00:04:21.660
Freedom begins by accepting differences Dance and create the universe

00:04:23.930 --> 00:04:29.410
In truth, I was sad until I met you

00:04:29.740 --> 00:04:35.720
I lied, thinking it was easier to be alone

00:04:35.720 --> 00:04:42.120
Even though we don’t like the same books or hobbies

00:04:42.120 --> 00:04:46.010
You’re the only one who agreed with me

00:04:46.010 --> 00:04:48.810
Joy and sadness and anger and do re mi fa so la ti do

00:04:48.810 --> 00:04:50.560
There’s no harmony and scenario without differences

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:54.600
Everyone is not the same

00:04:55.520 --> 00:04:58.690
That’s the reason for living

00:04:59.210 --> 00:05:04.860
Even if the sounds are dissonant at times

00:05:04.860 --> 00:05:09.920
That’s why I never give up
I believe my strength will get me through

00:05:10.790 --> 00:05:13.540
I travel to the edge of the world

00:05:13.950 --> 00:05:18.000
The sights I see with you are the truth

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:20.840
Whether it’s rain, wind, blizzard or the scorching sun

00:05:20.840 --> 00:05:24.090
They give color to each day
Will and love keep me from losing heart

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:27.080
Your kindness was harsh
I learned frustration when we clashed

00:05:27.080 --> 00:05:31.150
Freedom begins by accepting differences Dance and create the universe

00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:41.900
That was delicious, Kotori.

00:05:41.900 --> 00:05:47.530
\hBattle at Duel Sanctuary: Legendary Monsters Resurrect!!\h

00:05:41.900 --> 00:05:47.530
Number 15:

00:05:42.880 --> 00:05:45.310
I was about to die of starvation.

00:05:45.310 --> 00:05:47.530
Thank you, Haru.

00:05:47.960 --> 00:05:49.220
Haru?

00:05:49.220 --> 00:05:51.240
What’s your relationship with my grandmother?

00:05:52.790 --> 00:05:57.600
Haru helps me with various things.

00:05:59.690 --> 00:06:01.650
What’s with this old man?

00:06:01.650 --> 00:06:03.000
Don’t call me an old man!

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:07.920
I’m Rokujuro, the owner
of this duel sanctuary.

00:06:09.280 --> 00:06:11.300
Duel sanctuary?

00:06:13.560 --> 00:06:16.540
You sent Yuma to a duel sanctuary?

00:06:16.540 --> 00:06:17.980
Why?

00:06:17.980 --> 00:06:22.540
I’ve said over and over that it’s dangerous to get Yuma more involved in dueling.

00:06:22.540 --> 00:06:24.440
Dad did too!

00:06:24.440 --> 00:06:32.240
Though he’s inexperienced, he can find his true goal through dueling.

00:06:32.240 --> 00:06:33.660
True goal?

00:06:34.650 --> 00:06:36.160
We can’t go home?

00:06:36.550 --> 00:06:41.580
That’s right. There are no more buses, and everyone goes to sleep at sunset.

00:06:41.580 --> 00:06:43.640
Oh no!

00:06:43.640 --> 00:06:46.090
You can sleep here if you want.

00:06:46.090 --> 00:06:49.050
Sleep here?

00:06:49.050 --> 00:06:52.260
We can’t sleep in such a filthy place!

00:06:53.350 --> 00:06:58.240
If a man doesn’t work, he doesn’t sleep.

00:06:58.240 --> 00:07:00.240
Hey, wait!

00:07:09.940 --> 00:07:12.820
Tetsuo, put them in the back.

00:07:13.710 --> 00:07:16.650
Yuma, stop goofing off!

00:07:16.650 --> 00:07:18.790
This is annoying.

00:07:18.790 --> 00:07:22.080
Why is the old man making us clean?

00:07:23.820 --> 00:07:27.440
The old man went through there.

00:07:35.870 --> 00:07:38.560
Dark Magician!

00:07:38.560 --> 00:07:41.560
Blue-Eyes White Dragon!

00:07:41.560 --> 00:07:43.270
Wow!

00:07:43.270 --> 00:07:46.640
Red-Eyes! Neos!

00:07:46.640 --> 00:07:49.360
Even Dark Magician Girl!

00:07:49.360 --> 00:07:52.910
The legendary monsters are all here!

00:07:52.910 --> 00:07:54.990
Wow!

00:07:54.990 --> 00:07:57.350
Yuma, stop goofing off—

00:07:57.350 --> 00:07:59.090
What is this place?

00:07:59.950 --> 00:08:02.330
Wow!

00:08:03.910 --> 00:08:05.380
Are you surprised?

00:08:05.790 --> 00:08:11.340
I put my soul into creating these
Duel Monsters wooden statues.

00:08:11.340 --> 00:08:16.050
Every time a student leaves my nest,
I build a wooden statue.

00:08:16.050 --> 00:08:17.080
Student?

00:08:17.080 --> 00:08:24.170
Yes. This duel sanctuary is a thriving and historical duel training house.

00:08:24.520 --> 00:08:28.710
Many famous duelists were raised here.

00:08:29.190 --> 00:08:31.110
Wow!

00:08:31.110 --> 00:08:34.450
These wooden monster statues
look like they can move!

00:08:34.930 --> 00:08:36.370
They do move.

00:08:36.370 --> 00:08:38.700
Wooden statues move?

00:08:38.700 --> 00:08:42.460
Yes. During a duel, of course.

00:08:43.870 --> 00:08:45.840
Do you want to test it out?

00:08:48.450 --> 00:08:50.900
D-Gazer set!

00:08:55.630 --> 00:08:58.220
AR Vision Link complete.

00:08:59.720 --> 00:09:01.560
Duel!

00:09:01.560 --> 00:09:07.270
Four legends are already
summoned to our fields.

00:09:07.270 --> 00:09:11.860
I have Blue-Eyes Statue Dragon
and Red-Eyes Statue Dragon.

00:09:11.860 --> 00:09:16.820
You have Statue Dark Magician
and Statue Dark Magician Girl.

00:09:17.430 --> 00:09:22.290
We’ll use wooden decks that I specially made for the duel sanctuary.

00:09:22.290 --> 00:09:27.250
The four legendary monsters are still wooden statues.

00:09:27.250 --> 00:09:30.920
Their powers are sealed away,
and they have 0 ATK.

00:09:30.920 --> 00:09:32.960
They can’t attack.

00:09:32.960 --> 00:09:34.350
What?

00:09:34.350 --> 00:09:36.260
I knew they couldn’t move!

00:09:36.260 --> 00:09:39.730
They can both move and not move.

00:09:39.730 --> 00:09:41.760
It’s up to you.

00:09:43.220 --> 00:09:45.840
Up to Yuma? I see.

00:09:45.840 --> 00:09:49.230
Everything depends
on the player’s decisions during a duel.

00:09:49.230 --> 00:09:52.770
Yuma, these monsters have effects.

00:09:52.770 --> 00:09:56.820
There must be a card in your deck
that is the key to everything.

00:09:56.820 --> 00:09:58.530
In my deck?

00:10:01.080 --> 00:10:02.490
I get it!

00:10:02.490 --> 00:10:04.860
What’s taking so long?

00:10:04.860 --> 00:10:06.540
You’re going first.

00:10:06.540 --> 00:10:09.040
All right, here I go!

00:10:09.040 --> 00:10:11.040
My turn! I draw!

00:10:12.510 --> 00:10:13.960
This is it!

00:10:13.960 --> 00:10:17.090
I activate the Field Spell Statue Zone!

00:10:19.410 --> 00:10:24.880
The Field Spell Statue Zone removes the seal on the statue monsters.

00:10:34.940 --> 00:10:37.780
Monsters, move!

00:11:09.310 --> 00:11:10.480
I did it!

00:11:11.110 --> 00:11:14.480
I made the legendary monsters move!

00:11:14.480 --> 00:11:18.690
Awesome! Red-Eyes and Blue-Eyes!

00:11:18.690 --> 00:11:21.500
All right! Go, Dark Magician!

00:11:21.500 --> 00:11:22.870
Attack Red-Eyes!

00:11:22.870 --> 00:11:24.980
Black Magic!

00:11:29.950 --> 00:11:32.120
Not bad.

00:11:32.120 --> 00:11:34.880
I did it! This is fun!

00:11:34.880 --> 00:11:40.220
But are you really moving the monsters?

00:11:41.510 --> 00:11:43.250
What are you talking about?

00:11:43.250 --> 00:11:46.140
Dark Magician just destroyed Red-Eyes!

00:11:46.920 --> 00:11:49.850
The real duel is only beginning.

00:11:58.340 --> 00:11:59.690
What?

00:12:07.190 --> 00:12:08.790
What’s this?

00:12:09.230 --> 00:12:10.710
Why?

00:12:12.540 --> 00:12:16.540
Why am I Dark Magician?

00:12:16.540 --> 00:12:19.830
I’ve turned into a monster?

00:12:25.840 --> 00:12:27.300
Impossible...

00:12:27.870 --> 00:12:30.270
What’s going on?

00:12:30.270 --> 00:12:33.230
I’ve turned into a monster?

00:12:33.230 --> 00:12:34.710
Here I go!

00:12:34.710 --> 00:12:36.360
It’s my turn!

00:12:36.360 --> 00:12:40.280
I activate the spell card Polymerization!

00:12:42.950 --> 00:12:49.230
I send three Blue-Eyes in my hand and on my field to the graveyard and fuse them together!

00:12:50.910 --> 00:12:53.790
C’mon, Fusion Summon!

00:12:53.790 --> 00:12:57.630
Blue-Eyes Ultimate Statue Dragon!

00:13:02.460 --> 00:13:03.660
Here I go!

00:13:03.660 --> 00:13:07.220
Ultimate Dragon attacks Dark Magician Girl!

00:13:08.250 --> 00:13:11.140
Ultimate Burst!

00:13:19.480 --> 00:13:22.310
Dark Magician Girl!

00:13:24.490 --> 00:13:29.200
I activate the Quick-Play Spell,
De-Fusion from my hand.

00:13:29.200 --> 00:13:36.210
I return the Fusion Monster to my Extra Deck, and I Special Summon its Fusion Material Monsters from the graveyard.

00:13:36.710 --> 00:13:41.160
Resurrect, three Blue-Eyes!

00:13:44.100 --> 00:13:46.130
Don’t do it!

00:13:46.130 --> 00:13:48.840
Don’t do it!

00:13:49.860 --> 00:13:51.800
That’s right.

00:13:51.800 --> 00:13:58.020
It’s natural to tremble in fear
when you face a powerful foe.

00:13:58.890 --> 00:14:00.520
Attack him!

00:14:00.520 --> 00:14:01.860
Galaxy-Eyes’s effect activates!

00:14:01.860 --> 00:14:03.360
What’s wrong?

00:14:03.360 --> 00:14:05.640
It’s the same for monsters.

00:14:05.640 --> 00:14:10.070
Monsters are always facing fear.

00:14:11.130 --> 00:14:12.280
Here I go!

00:14:12.280 --> 00:14:17.870
Three Blue-Eyes attack Dark Magician—
No, they attack Yuma!

00:14:17.870 --> 00:14:20.690
Burst Stream of Destruction!

00:14:34.350 --> 00:14:35.770
Yuma!

00:14:35.770 --> 00:14:38.850
Maybe I scared you too much.

00:14:40.400 --> 00:14:44.110
You felt a monster’s fear.

00:14:44.540 --> 00:14:48.740
That means you understand how a monster feels.

00:14:48.740 --> 00:14:56.410
Your desire to answer the monsters’ feelings will truly move a monster.

00:14:57.050 --> 00:15:01.040
Learn how they feel
and respond to their feelings...

00:15:01.040 --> 00:15:07.740
Monsters also feel fear,
but they try to overcome it.

00:15:22.730 --> 00:15:24.150
Hey, Yuma!

00:15:24.680 --> 00:15:28.110
Yuma, how long are you staying here?

00:15:28.750 --> 00:15:30.770
If you want to go home, then leave.

00:15:30.770 --> 00:15:32.890
I’m going to stay here a little longer.

00:15:34.320 --> 00:15:37.650
Then I’m going to make breakfast!

00:15:37.650 --> 00:15:39.040
Hey!

00:15:49.900 --> 00:15:52.010
What’s this scratch?

00:15:52.010 --> 00:15:55.470
Who would do something so horrible?

00:15:56.020 --> 00:15:59.200
It was repaired after it was cut in half.

00:16:07.230 --> 00:16:12.740
That boy has the ability to shine.

00:16:12.740 --> 00:16:15.660
He’s the complete opposite of him.

00:16:27.630 --> 00:16:29.510
You...

00:16:29.510 --> 00:16:31.400
I’m back.

00:16:34.590 --> 00:16:36.030
Master.

00:16:37.950 --> 00:16:41.020
Master, I’m back.

00:16:41.020 --> 00:16:45.480
Yamikawa, you’re darker than before.

00:16:46.050 --> 00:16:50.030
I’ll pull you into the darkness.

00:16:54.630 --> 00:16:55.960
Duel!

00:17:05.920 --> 00:17:08.630
Who are you?

00:17:09.850 --> 00:17:11.260
Who are you?

00:17:12.900 --> 00:17:14.220
Yuma...

00:17:14.870 --> 00:17:16.010
Old man?

00:17:16.010 --> 00:17:17.680
Run away, Yuma!

00:17:18.190 --> 00:17:19.780
Run away?

00:17:19.780 --> 00:17:21.640
Who is he?

00:17:21.640 --> 00:17:24.530
He’s my former student.

00:17:32.460 --> 00:17:35.880
Why do you desire darkness?

00:17:35.880 --> 00:17:40.620
Power without light will destroy you!

00:17:46.290 --> 00:17:47.960
Yamikawa, what are you doing?

00:17:54.110 --> 00:17:56.720
I’ll be back!

00:18:01.950 --> 00:18:08.580
When I do, I’ll defeat you and take the duel sanctuary’s legendary deck!

00:18:11.040 --> 00:18:13.420
I defeated you.

00:18:13.420 --> 00:18:15.860
Where’s the duel sanctuary’s legendary deck?

00:18:16.290 --> 00:18:18.320
I won’t give it to you.

00:18:18.320 --> 00:18:19.660
What?

00:18:19.660 --> 00:18:21.550
You still don’t understand?

00:18:21.550 --> 00:18:24.290
You’re a fool whose soul
has been taken over by darkness!

00:18:29.920 --> 00:18:33.350
Then I’ll slash everything!

00:18:33.350 --> 00:18:34.590
Stop it!

00:18:35.150 --> 00:18:36.690
What are you doing?

00:18:38.780 --> 00:18:40.530
Who are you?

00:18:40.530 --> 00:18:42.780
Why are you stopping me?

00:18:42.780 --> 00:18:44.560
I... I...

00:18:44.560 --> 00:18:47.480
I’m the old man’s student!

00:18:47.480 --> 00:18:49.140
Yuma...

00:18:49.790 --> 00:18:52.790
That senile fool’s student? You make me laugh.

00:18:52.790 --> 00:18:55.790
I won’t forgive anyone who insults my master!

00:18:55.790 --> 00:18:57.290
Interesting.

00:18:57.290 --> 00:18:59.450
I’ll swallow you in darkness!

00:18:59.450 --> 00:19:01.950
Duel Disk set!

00:19:07.160 --> 00:19:09.160
D-Gazer set!

00:19:12.140 --> 00:19:14.640
AR Vision Link complete.

00:19:15.480 --> 00:19:16.690
Duel!

00:19:17.340 --> 00:19:19.800
Do your best, Yuma.

00:19:19.800 --> 00:19:22.650
Yuma, I’ll fight too.

00:19:23.400 --> 00:19:25.510
Aren’t you supposed to be depressed?

00:19:26.070 --> 00:19:30.730
I learned from the old man,
so I’m also his student.

00:19:30.730 --> 00:19:32.810
I’ll go first!

00:19:33.330 --> 00:19:35.440
My turn! I draw!

00:19:35.830 --> 00:19:38.400
I summon Gagaga Magician!

00:19:42.360 --> 00:19:45.830
I set one card and end my turn!

00:19:45.830 --> 00:19:47.820
My turn.

00:19:47.820 --> 00:19:49.300
I draw!

00:19:49.300 --> 00:19:51.350
I summon Flame Armor Ninja!

00:19:56.020 --> 00:20:01.610
I activate the spell card Armor Ninjitsu Art of Teleporation from my hand!

00:20:03.030 --> 00:20:09.680
I Special Summon one monster from my hand that has equal or fewer ATK than Flame Armor Ninja!

00:20:09.680 --> 00:20:12.580
Appear, Air Armor Ninja!

00:20:14.200 --> 00:20:19.360
Due to Teleportation’s effect, Flame and Air can’t attack. However...

00:20:19.360 --> 00:20:21.700
Two Level 4 monsters!

00:20:21.700 --> 00:20:26.380
I overlay Level 4 Flame Armor Ninja
and Air Armor Ninja!

00:20:27.200 --> 00:20:30.140
With these two monsters,
I build the Overlay Network.

00:20:30.140 --> 00:20:31.910
Xyz Summon!

00:20:31.910 --> 00:20:35.500
Appear, Blade Armor Ninja!

00:20:39.560 --> 00:20:42.610
He already summoned a Xyz Monster!

00:20:42.610 --> 00:20:45.050
He’s fast. He’s exceptional.

00:20:45.050 --> 00:20:49.320
Blade Armor Ninja attacks Gagaga Magician!

00:20:51.770 --> 00:20:54.270
I flip over my Continuous Trap!

00:20:54.270 --> 00:20:55.950
Gagaga Shield!

00:20:55.950 --> 00:21:00.540
This card equips on to a Spellcaster-Type monster.

00:21:00.540 --> 00:21:02.440
I equip it on Gagaga Magician!

00:21:02.440 --> 00:21:05.670
Slash, Electromagnetic Sword!

00:21:06.840 --> 00:21:09.120
Mist Slash!

00:21:09.120 --> 00:21:13.800
Gagaga Shield protects Gagaga Magician from being destroyed in battle twice!

00:21:13.800 --> 00:21:16.540
But you’ll feel its sharpness.

00:21:20.050 --> 00:21:28.470
Once per turn, Blade Armor Ninja can use an Overlay Unit to attack again!

00:21:31.470 --> 00:21:33.810
Feel its sharpness again!

00:21:35.280 --> 00:21:36.980
Yuma!

00:21:39.330 --> 00:21:40.500
You fool.

00:21:40.500 --> 00:21:44.690
If you didn’t try to protect your monster, you wouldn’t have taken damage.

00:21:45.090 --> 00:21:47.490
Monsters are my friends.

00:21:47.490 --> 00:21:51.010
My friends are overcoming
their fears to battle!

00:21:51.010 --> 00:21:54.910
So I’ll protect my friends to the end!

00:21:54.910 --> 00:21:57.100
Friends? Pathetic.

00:21:57.100 --> 00:22:01.850
I’ll slash your ideas and your monster in half!

00:22:01.850 --> 00:22:03.190
Whatever!

00:22:03.190 --> 00:22:06.940
I won’t let you do that!

00:22:12.470 --> 00:22:15.120
Let’s start the duel!

00:22:15.120 --> 00:22:17.370
This week’s quiz:

00:22:17.370 --> 00:22:20.870
How many cards are in your hand
at the start of a duel?

00:22:20.870 --> 00:22:24.540
4? 5? Or 6?

00:22:30.130 --> 00:22:34.760
Today’s test is hard
Can’t avoid pleasure and temptation

00:22:34.760 --> 00:22:39.600
I want to go home and watch TV
Recent cartoons are entertaining

00:22:49.890 --> 00:22:54.320
Anyway, tests are hard
Language, math and English are especially hard

00:22:54.320 --> 00:22:59.560
Average scores in science and social studies
I’m only good at P.E.

00:22:59.560 --> 00:23:01.980
(Wait, Baby!) The expected

00:23:01.980 --> 00:23:04.630
(What’s that, Baby!) Answers

00:23:04.630 --> 00:23:06.990
(Wait a sec, Baby!) Remember them

00:23:06.990 --> 00:23:08.900
(What are we!? Baby!) For who

00:23:08.900 --> 00:23:13.510
Let’s say I wrote the correct answers on that sheet

00:23:13.510 --> 00:23:18.120
Will that change the future a year or a decade from now?

00:23:18.160 --> 00:23:23.440
The world I drew at the edge of dreams

00:23:23.440 --> 00:23:28.190
Someday I’ll race in the sky

00:23:28.190 --> 00:23:33.300
Nobody can threaten my heart

00:23:33.300 --> 00:23:37.030
Nothing is correct!

00:23:40.060 --> 00:23:43.330
Yamikawa is the old man’s former student.

00:23:43.330 --> 00:23:46.380
He masterfully uses his ninja deck to corner me!

00:23:46.380 --> 00:23:51.450
He’s willing to sacrifice his monsters to attain victory.

00:23:51.450 --> 00:23:52.780
This duel is scary.

00:23:53.180 --> 00:23:54.370
Yuma, you must believe!

00:23:54.370 --> 00:23:58.310
Yeah! The monsters are my
friends who battle alongside me!

00:23:58.310 --> 00:24:01.790
I’ll trust and protect my friends and fight!

00:24:01.790 --> 00:24:10.010
\h\hSpecial Ninjitsu Art! The Mightiest Ninja Appears!\h\h

00:24:01.790 --> 00:24:06.880
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ZEXAL:
“Special Ninjitsu Art! The Mightiest Ninja Appears!”

00:24:07.360 --> 00:24:10.010
I’m kattobing!

00:24:11.860 --> 00:24:14.160
The answer is... 5!

00:24:14.160 --> 00:24:18.000
The top five cards in your deck become your hand.

00:24:18.000 --> 00:24:20.250
Then start the duel!

00:24:20.250 --> 00:24:24.420
If you’re going first, don’t forget to draw!
